## Why This Is Asked

Tests on-device few-shot adaptation, robust 3D pose in a cluttered retail environment, and strict latency constraints, plus ongoing data drift with weekly new items.

## Key Concepts

- On-device few-shot adaptation with prototypes
- 6-DoF pose from monocular RGB
- Temporal tracking with Kalman filter and data association
- Domain randomization for synthetic-real data
- Efficiency-focused backbone and head design

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-architecture sketch
class PoseHead {
  forward(featROI, box) {
    const phi = mlp(featROI, 128)
    const q = normalize(phi.slice(0,4))
    const t = phi.slice(4,7)
    return { q, t }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you disambiguate symmetric items (e.g., round cans) in pose estimation?
- How would you measure latency and ensure stable 50 ms/frame under thermal throttling?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests system-level thinking for 3D reconstruction under dynamic scenes and edge-runtime constraints, plus evaluation rigor.

## Key Concepts

- Dense 3D representation (TSDF) with dynamic masking
- Lightweight pose estimation and masked fusion
- Dynamic voxel confidence and decay for occlusions
- Edge latency targets and robust evaluation metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: update TSDF with dynamic masking
function updateVoxelTSDF(voxel, depth, pose, isDynamic) {
  if (isDynamic) return; // skip static updates for dynamic voxels until confirmed
  const sdf = projectDepthToVoxel(depth, pose, voxel.coord);
  voxel.tsdf = (voxel.tsdf * voxel.weight + sdf) / (voxel.weight + 1);
  voxel.weight += 1;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you integrate semantic priors to improve dynamic masking in cluttered warehouses?
- What ablation model would you run to measure the impact of dynamic masking on map quality and drift over 5 seconds?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses on-device CV design, latency budgeting, and robust 3D human pose estimation for safety-critical driving.

## Key Concepts
- On-device real-time inference with a lightweight backbone
- 2D-to-3D pose reconstruction and Kalman filtering
- Self-supervised pretraining from unlabeled video
- Robustness to occlusion and adverse weather
- Quantization and latency accounting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for pipeline
class PedestrianPoseEstimator {
  constructor() { /* load detector, 3D head, PnP module, tracker */ }
  forward(frame) {
    const keypoints2D = this.detector.detect(frame)
    const pose3D = this.poseHead.estimate(keypoints2D)
    const pose6DoF = differentiablePnP(pose3D, this.cameraIntrinsics)
    return this.tracker.update(pose6DoF)
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to multi-pedestrian tracking with identity preservation?
- What failure modes are most critical in heavy rain and how would you mitigate them?
